#raw("STATE\nYou move one cell per turn: north (up), south (down), east (right) or west (left). Walls (#) block you, and walking into one wastes the move. Stepping onto the key (K) picks it up. A locked door (D) opens when you walk into it carrying the key, and you step through; without the key it blocks you like a wall. Reaching the goal (G) wins.\n\nMap, with column numbers along the top and row numbers down the side (# = wall, . = floor, A = you, G = goal, K = key, D = locked door). A position (x, y) is column x, row y:\n   0123456789\n 0 ##########\n 1 #......A.#\n 2 #..##..K.#\n 3 #D....#..#\n 4 #G#.#...##\n 5 ##########\n\nYou are A at (7, 1). You are carrying nothing.\nObjects: goal G at (1, 4); key K at (7, 2); locked door D at (1, 3).\n\nQUESTION\nWhat is the best next move?\n\nOPTIONS\noption_1: move south (down)\noption_2: move north (up)\noption_3: move west (left)\noption_4: move east (right)", block: true, lang: "text")
